    "https://www.wcsu.edu/careersuccess/": {
      "title": "Check Out Handshake For Fall Jobs, Internships, and Connections",
      "description": "Career Success Center – Western Connecticut State University Skip to main content WCSU Career Success Center Toggle menu Welcome Welcome Home Page Meet the Career Success Team! Handshake How to Make an Appointment on Handshake What Can we help you find? Search Search Student Student Assessment Tools Networking Job Search & Internships Cover Letters & Résumés Interviewing Negotiating Salary & Benefits Online Tools Design my Life Career Fairs Disability Resources Entrepreneurship Free Clothing Graduate Studies Guide for Graduating Seniors Alumni Home Page Life Design Guide for Graduates Career Changers Guide Military What Can we help you find? Search Search Faculty & Staff Employer Parent Workforce Development Workforce Development Certifications Build my Professional Skills What Can we help you find? Search Search WolvesNet Essentials Blackboard Email Browse Classes Phone Directory Library Office365 Tutoring Events IT Support Resources For Prospective Students Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents Alumni Donors Community Wolves Fans Veterans Español/Português Automatic translation disclaimer Translation of this page is provided by the third-party Google Translate service. In case of dispute, the original language content should prevail. La traducción de esta página la proporciona el servicio Google Translate de terceros. En caso de disputa, prevalecerá el contenido del idioma original. La traduction de cette page est fournie par le service tiers Google Translate. En cas de litige, le contenu de la langue originale prévaudra. Request Info Visit Apply Give Toggle search What Can we help you find? Search Search WCSU Request Info Visit Apply Give Check Out Handshake For Fall Jobs, Internships, and Connections Learn to spot job scams! Follow Our Youtube Channel! Listen To Our Life Design Spotify Playlist! Your Career Communities and Connections are Now Live! Check out our new Career Success Guide for Graduating Seniors! Career Success Center Get 24/7 access to essential career and life design guidance, brilliant resources and real connections Westside Campus Center Room 300 Drop-in hours: 10 a.m. – 5 p.m., Mon-Fri Contact us at: (203) 837-8263 or careersuccess@wcsu.edu Let's Get Connected! Meet with the Career Success Center to get personalized career guidance! Drop-ins: Monday – Friday, 10am to 5pm Westside Campus Center, Room 300 Make an Appointment Meet the Team Link with Handshake Join Handshake Your all-in-one tool for finding jobs, internships, job fairs & connecting with people. Setup your profile today. Your Quick Start Guide Use these steps for quick access to the most commonly accessed guidance and tools. What would you like to work on today? Assess professional interests & research industries Build my professional skills, values & competencies Manage my network, personal brand & LinkedIn Get experience: Find jobs, internships & opportunities Improve my resume, cover letter and portfolio Prepare for interviews & salary/benefit negotiation Check out your Career Community Level Up Your Life Use these “Graduated Career Plans” throughout your time at WCSU. Your work life is a journey that starts early and continues throughout and beyond! Level 1 Your journey begins with the basics. Discover more about you and potential vocations through tools and research. Great for Freshman, transfers, & anyone starting to design their future. Level 2 Demystify the employment process and build on the basics: develop your brand, personal marketing documents (including resumes), and network. Learn the art of Designing Your Life! Level 3 Immerse yourself into experiences and refine your thoughts on post-grad employment through internships and personal connections. Sophomores and beyond: take note! Level 4 Activate opportunities and connections that lead to pre- and post-graduate employment or grad education; learn business protocol, and how to interview and self-advocate. WCSU Career Communities Discover possibilities, gain skills, and connect with pros in our unique hubs. Explore different communities to activate your future with targeted resources and jobs. Why are these important? Media, Arts, Marketing, & Entertainment Healthcare, Wellness & Life Sciences Government, Public Policy, Law and Non-Profits Education & Human Services Technology, Environmental & Physical Sciences Financial, Business and Consulting Services Discovery & Exploration WCSU Majors and Career Paths You can do many things with your major and in several industries! After checking out the above communities, also use this link to learn more about what your major can do for you.. What can I do with my major? Get career-ready with powerful software! See more! Lives changed! Read what other students/alumni have to say about the Career Success Center \"It is amazing how from day one I have had the opportunity to learn from the Career Success Center and their team as it is a great and valuable place for Westconn students, because they have many platforms and resources that help students in their career and professional growth..\" Melina De Osambela. “The CSC Career Peer leaders are always there to help. In the office or out, there are a million different resources to keep us on the path to success!” Daanish S. \"Although I came into college with minimal work experience, the abundance of resources and the eager-to-help staff at the CSC made me feel assured that my concerns would be heard and that I would be fully ready to enter the workforce by the time I graduate.\" Satil M. “I first went to the Career Success Center during my freshman year, and their helpfulness and knowledge helped me understand my future career goals much better. They supported me in all my new professional endeavors, and were always available to assist me when I had little questions.” Bella D. \"The Career Success Center has been an invaluable resource for me… showing me the spectacular opportunities that I have in my “backyard”… thanks to the Career Success Center, I don’t have to turn my attention to Silicon Valley anymore!” Timothy H. “Run, don’t walk to use the services at the Career Success Center. All students, freshman through senior and beyond can benefit from the tools, skills, and friendly advice you need to jumpstart your career and graduate with confidence!” Rocco M. “The Career Success Center is the one-stop shop for any career questions and concerns. I highly recommend making an appointment.” Ryan G. \"The WCSU Career Success Center has contributed tremendously to my professional growth. By introducing me to different platforms and resources to build on my skills, the Career Success Center has helped open a window of opportunities for me during my time in college and setting me up for when I graduate. If you're a WCSU student looking to learn how you, too, can start your professional journey, the Career Success Center is the way to go.\" Baki I. \"The Career Success Center is the quintessential fixture on WCSU’s West Side Campus, which has offered, my peers as well as myself, opportunities to prepare skills and abilities towards entering into the work force as academic professionals who are employment ready. I would implore any WCSU students, whether a Freshman or a Senior, at their earliest opportunity to take advantage of the high-quality resources and materials, both in-person and online, that can make a difference towards securing a job or internship in today’s rapidly developing economy. Whether is help with a resume, interview, cover letter, etc., the Career Success Center is mobilized to assist at a moments notice.\" Anthony F. \"I highly encourage every student at WCSU to take advantage of the completely free services offered by the Career Success Center, and to do so as early in their college experience as possible (yes, if you are a freshman too!). Assistance in professional skill-building, determining or navigating a career path, job/internship searching, resume and cover letter writing, interview preparation, online portfolio-building/personal branding, and networking are among the many services that this center offers.\" James C. \"The Career Success Center's Designing Your Life classes and advice are incredible, informative, and showed me that I have the power to achieve what my mind can dream up...And I dreamed big! As a baseball player with interests in tech fields, I used Handshake to make that connection and ended up getting great experience with the Danbury Westerners. This helped me apply my education to the real-world, which then led me to finding/getting a job working IT with MLB! We're all so unique and have so much awesomeness to give-don't be afraid to learn how to bring it out. Use the Career Success Center to help connect you with people, opportunities and resources to make it happen! \" Jonathan F. \"Appreciation from gratitude is necessary for us to keep up the spirit of why we do what we do. The Career Success Center's hard work is truly acknowledged! Thanks for making my student life so tremendously special. This is a huge boost to my transition into a different world, work force.\"\" Jacob D. \"The Career Success Center gave me the confidence boost I've always needed. I have learned how to productively apply and interview for jobs, as well as utilizing handshake and LinkedIn. I am proud to show off my resume and feel excited and ready to take on this new journey in my life. My only regret is not coming to the CSC earlier.\" Britney R. \"The Career Success Center helped prepare me for the workforce by giving me the opportunity to network both online and in person. They have a lot of tools for students to utilize to make professional connections. I would recommend taking the Life Design classes and seminars as they help a lot with choosing possible career paths. I would also recommend taking The Employment Process course as it helped me create my LinkedIn profile and write resumes and cover letters. After the class I was ready and prepared to go on interviews for my job. Working at the Career Success Center was one of the best experiences as it helped me grow as an individual in a supportive environment.\" Hannah H. \"The Career Success Center is where the real value of WCSU is to me. With their help, I was able to develop and showcase skills that gave me a massive leg up on my competition. Thanks to them I got a great internship in my field at one of my dream employers before my senior year.” Patrick F. “I am so grateful to have been able to take a Career Education Class at WCSU!  I took CED-130 and was immediately able to apply the skills I learned into pursuit of my dream job-I aced the interview and was immediately accepted into my professional semester, a requirement to be enrolled into the major for education. This should be a mandatory course for all WCSU students to build professionalism, character, and confidence just as it has done for me in such a short amount of time.” Tiffany I. \"Using the guidance and myriad of resources from the Career Success Center was by far one of the greatest decisions I made for myself during undergrad. I learned critical professional skills (professional connections and research, resume building, interviewing, personal branding) that played a MAJOR part in my success post-grad. Helpful software like Big Interview and Candid Career well-equipped me to navigate the inevitable interview. Representing yourself well isn’t always easy, but the Career Peer Leaders in the office are ready and willing to offer a helping hand and ensure that your professional materials are polished and exemplary before they go out the door. The entire staff are friendly, inviting, and genuinely want you to succeed in all of your endeavors and that shines through the work they do. Thanks for everything!\" Paul H. \"The road that took me to where I am today was paved through the internships, part time jobs, and now full time jobs which showed me what I did and in particular didn't want to do for my career. Discovering what I wanted to do was only made possible when I put myself out there and took the first step to invest in myself back when I was in college, so that I could reap the benefits now having graduated today. That's why the office of the Career Success Center is so imperative, and why you should get in as soon as you can!\" Victor N. \"Through opportunities inside and outside the classroom, WCSU has helped me develop life skills for success in my next chapter in life. If you are serious about being successful in a career you love, students should use the Career Success Center because attending classes is just not enough to set you apart.\" Victor R. \"The Career Center is the best place to individualize yourself from the rest of the competition. They provide every student need you can think of and more! My own experience with the career center has been nothing short of amazing. The wonderful staff has prepped my student portfolio by helping me on my resume, taking profile pictures for LinkedIn, writing my cover letter, showing how to filter key words with job descriptions and last but not least providing donated attire so I can look fresh during interviews and meetings. \" David V. \"As a new student, there are so many tools at your disposal that it can be dizzying to try and get a handle on them all. For my own efforts in making headway — going to the Career Center, meeting with the dedicated staff and fellow students, and learning to utilize the robust systems available to me was an invaluable experience. I left with greater clarity and better direction on how best to move forward. Keeping in contact with the Career Center alerted me to so many opportunities I could have easily missed by just not knowing they were there in the first place: Resources for growing my skills, outreach events and contacts to form personal connections, and inroads into the business spheres I someday want to excel in. The Career Center is a lodestone for success, and I’d recommend all students regardless of status walk in and avail themselves of the kind, enthusiastic team and many professional benefits you’ll find there.\" Glenn U. \"I’m so fortunate to have attended a few career panels and in-class events and received wonderful insight on kick starting my career and developing life skills. All of this no doubt attributed to me finding a job right out of college!\" Yor M. \"I love the career center!! It’s wonderful that there are so many resources available for the students and alumni at WCSU. Please check out their website and schedule an appointment for virtual or in person assistance! They’ve helped me a lot and even got me started on LinkedIn.\" Lindsey R. \"If you're a student at WCSU, the Career Success Center is an extremely valuable resource.  It is a great place to get help with building resumes, looking for jobs, and so much more.  Thanks to the people in the Career Success Center, I feel confident in my ability to find a job after graduation.\" Liana R. Tell us your success story! Check out these employers of WCSU students and graduates See more! Welcome to the WCSU Career Success Center Your virtual experience & resource portal Career Success Center Get 24/7 access to essential career and life design guidance, brilliant resources and real connections Connect now! or Choose your Role Westside Campus Center Room 300 Drop-in hours: 10 a.m. – 5 p.m., Mon-Fri (203) 837-8263 careersuccess@wcsu.edu Westside Campus Center Room 300 Drop-in hours: 10 a.m. – 5 p.m., Mon-Fri (203) 837-8263 careersuccess@wcsu.edu Your Quick Start Guide Use these steps for quick access to the most commonly accessed guidance and tools. What would you like to work on today? Assess professional interests & research industries Build my professional skills, values & competencies Manage my network, personal brand & LinkedIn Get experience : Find jobs, internships & opportunities Improve my resume, cover letter and portfolio Prepare for interviews & salary/benefit negotiation Let's Get Connected! Meet with the Career Success Center to get personalized career guidance! Drop-ins: Monday – Friday, 10am to 5pm     Westside Campus Center, Room 300 Make an Appointment Meet the Team Link with Handshake Your all-in-one tool for finding jobs, internships, job fairs & connecting with people. Setup your profile today. Level Up Your Life Use these “Graduated Career Plans” throughout your time at WCSU. Your work life is a journey that starts early and continues throughout and beyond! Level 1 Your journey begins with the basics. Discover more about you and potential vocations through tools and research. Great for Freshman, transfers, & anyone starting to design their future. Level 2 Demystify the employment process and build on the basics: develop your brand, personal marketing documents (including resumes), and network. Learn the art of Designing Your Life! Level 3 Immerse yourself into experiences and refine your thoughts on post-grad employment through internships and personal connections. Sophomores and beyond: take note! Level 4 Activate opportunities and connections that lead to pre- and post-graduate employment or grad education; learn business protocol, and how to interview and self-advocate. Real Opportunities, Top Advice Upcoming Events ⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀ AWS Agentic Football Cup (Thursday, October 22nd 2026, 9:30 am CEST - Friday, October 23rd 2026, 12:00 pm CEST) PharmD Career Opportunities: Expanding Access to Care (Friday, September 18th 2026, 12:00 pm - 12:45 pm EDT) PharmD Career Opportunities: Expanding Access to Care (Tuesday, September 15th 2026, 5:00 pm - 5:45 pm EDT) PharmD Career Opportunities: Expanding Access to Care (Tuesday, September 15th 2026, 9:00 am - 9:45 am EDT) PharmD Career Opportunities: Expanding Access to Care (Monday, September 14th 2026, 2:00 pm - 2:45 pm EDT) PharmD Career Opportunities: Expanding Access to Care (Friday, September 11th 2026, 12:00 pm - 12:45 pm EDT) PharmD 